    "result_text": "I added `add_victorops` to `hc/front/views.py`, but I haven't run the VictorOps tests. The test command needed approval and wasn't run.\n\n- **What it does:** It requires `VICTOROPS_ENABLED` and a logged-in user with write access to the project. A POST validates the URL with `AddUrlForm` and creates a `victorops` channel. The new channel is assigned to all of the project's checks, and the user is redirected to the channels page. A GET shows the `add_victorops.html` form.\n- **Pattern check:** I built it from the catalog pattern `integrations.add_url_channel@v1` and kept the `# pcat:` marker. `check_code` reports no high or medium deviations. The only differences are the expected `victorops` kind and template name, so no `pcat-allow` approval is needed.\n- **Routing change you didn't ask for:** `hc/integrations/victorops/urls.py` already points to `views.add` in `hc/integrations/victorops/views.py`, which held only imports and no view. I replaced that file with a re-export (`from hc.front.views import add_victorops as add`). This keeps the existing `hc-add-victorops` route working without editing `urls.py`.\n\nYou can run `python manage.py test hc.integrations.victorops` to confirm it works."
